# Every text file is stored with LF. Scripts and manifests are also checked out with LF on Windows (core.autocrlf=true would give CRLF):
# a PowerShell here-string sent over ssh carries the checkout's line ends to the VM, where bash reads each `\r` as part of the command
# (Test-HostBaseline's AppArmor probe failed that way from a CRLF checkout, plan 08 Task 12 push report). Invoke-HostedSsh strips `\r`
# too; this keeps every checkout byte-identical to what was reviewed.
* text=auto
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.tpl text eol=lf
*.lua text eol=lf
*.tf text eol=lf
*.hcl text eol=lf
